    <tags>database schema migration sql-server postgresql mysql cli devops admin</tags>
    <summary>Schema package management CLI tools for SQL Server, PostgreSQL, and MySQL.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[
SchemaSmith is a state-based database schema management toolset for SQL Server, PostgreSQL, and MySQL. Define your desired database state as metadata — tables, views, procedures, indexes, foreign keys — and SchemaSmith transforms any target database to match.

This package installs three self-contained command-line tools:

- **schemaquench** — Deploys schema packages to a target database. Computes the exact DDL needed to bring the target in line with the package definition, with WhatIf analysis, idempotent deployments, and 9 ordered execution slots for fine-grained control.
- **schematongs** — Extracts a live database schema into a deployable package. Pure SQL extraction (no SMO), preserves subfolder organization, validates scripts post-extraction, detects orphans.
- **datatongs** — Extracts table data and generates idempotent MERGE scripts. Auto-detects primary keys, supports complex types, tokenized output for cross-environment reuse.

The canonical workflow is `schematongs` → review/edit → `schemaquench` (extract → review → apply). Tools share the same package format and ship on synchronized versions.

Self-contained binaries — no .NET runtime install required. Authenticode-signed via Azure Trusted Signing.

Documentation: https://schemasmith.com/
Source: https://github.com/Schema-Smith/SchemaSmith
License: SSCL v2.0 (https://github.com/Schema-Smith/SchemaSmith/blob/main/LICENSE)
]]></description>
    <releaseNotes>https://github.com/Schema-Smith/SchemaSmith/releases/tag/v__VERSION__</releaseNotes>
  </metadata>
  <files>
